<title>SWITZERLAND: Novartis sees higher 1997 profitability.</title>
<headline>Novartis sees higher 1997 profitability.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Life sciences group Novartis AG expects profitability to improve in 1997, chief executive Daniel Vasella said.</p>
<p>The outlook is based on a number of factors, including merger synergies, higher volumes, a positive currency effect and higher net liquidity, he said at the company's annual shareholders meeting.  </p>
<p>In response to a question, Novartis Chairman Alex Krauer said the group was using a dollar exchange rate of 1.20 Swiss francs in its budget planning for 1997.</p>
<p>The dollar was quoted today at around 1.4520 francs.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
